.TH KUPI 1 "2026" "kupi 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kupi \- universal drag-and-drop package installer for Kali Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kupi
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kupi
opens a single window with a drag-and-drop zone. Drop a Linux package file
onto it (or pass one on the command line) and it detects the type, shows what
it will do, and \- on an explicit Install click \- runs the matching install
commands while streaming their terminal output live.
.PP
Supported types: Debian packages (\fB.deb\fR, via apt), RPM packages
(\fB.rpm\fR, via alien), AppImages (\fB.AppImage\fR: run in place or install to
~/Applications), self-extracting installers (\fB.run\fR, \fB.bin\fR), shell
installer scripts (\fB.sh\fR), tar and zip archives (extracted and scanned for
an install script or bundled .deb), snaps (\fB.snap\fR) and flatpaks
(\fB.flatpak\fR, \fB.flatpakref\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I FILE
Optional package file to preload into the window at startup.
.SH NOTES
Privilege escalation uses
.BR pkexec (1),
which shows a native polkit prompt. Cancelling a running install kills the
process that was started; a privileged child spawned via pkexec may keep
running to completion.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Applications
Default destination when installing an AppImage.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/kupi-*.desktop
Launchers written for installed AppImages.
.SH AUTHOR
Hashir Ahmad <hashirahmad8055@gmail.com>
